Patents Rules, 2024 - Rule 24C: Expedited examination of applications.
(1) An applicant may file a request for expedited examination in Form 18A on any of the following grounds:
(b) that the applicant is a Startup as defined under the startup India initiative;
(c) that the applicant is a small entity / Micro, Small and Medium Enterprise (MSME);
(f) that the applicant is a female applicant, or in case of joint applicants, where at least one applicant is a female;
(h) that the applicant is eligible under an arrangement between the Indian Patent Office and a foreign Patent Office (PPH).
Under Rule 24C, patent applications in Ayurveda or biotechnology filed by recognized MSMEs or Startups are assigned fast-track First Examination Reports (FER) within 60 to 90 days, significantly accelerating the patent prosecution timeline.
